  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14193353/assets/56a341e4982e2b91772399c81b9cef0df394320b1c640bec43ab0f39ab973143.png)\n\nThe graph of $y={f}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of a continuous function $f(x),$ is given above. Find all the values of $x$ where the function $f(x)$ has a local extremum. You may assume that all of the $x$-intercepts of $y={f}^{′}(x)$ are shown in the picture.",
